WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Build a sell-in timeline tracker with retailer-specific deadlines and contacts for our pumpkin spice lunch.

00:07.000 --> 00:17.000
Free Wishes is a better-free breakfast cereal. It is higher protein, lower in sugar, gluten and grain free.

00:17.000 --> 00:21.000
And the inspiration came from our own house and our own family.

00:21.000 --> 00:26.000
This one I didn't really create, but I thought of the flavor. It's called cotton candy.

00:26.000 --> 00:29.000
Not trying to glaze myself. Personally, my favorite.

00:29.000 --> 00:31.000
We're a true team in all the things that we do.

00:31.000 --> 00:33.000
But there's only so much two people can do.

00:33.000 --> 00:38.000
As you grow and the brand becomes bigger, mistakes just have so much more weight.

00:38.000 --> 00:43.000
In the past, it's so many tech ideas. But I always said, I can't do them. I need a technical co-founder.

00:43.000 --> 00:45.000
Codex is that technical co-founder.

00:45.000 --> 00:48.000
Every time we've had to run our seasonals, they become an operational nightmare.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.000
So we had Codex built this really beautiful command center and dashboard.

00:52.000 --> 00:56.000
So I always start by saying, please set a goal for yourself to do this end-to-end.

00:56.000 --> 01:00.000
Please use historical launches as a means to inform the dashboard itself.

01:00.000 --> 01:05.000
Use the Three Wishes branding, especially the new branding. We have new boxes that we're using.

01:05.000 --> 01:07.000
It is the most disorganized thought stream that I've ever seen.

01:07.000 --> 01:08.000
Totally. No, I got it.

01:08.000 --> 01:11.000
To them, it's like incredibly amazing output.

01:11.000 --> 01:13.000
I mean, it wouldn't have been possible before.

01:13.000 --> 01:19.000
With 5.6, I directed at some of Three Wishes brand guidelines and said, just make it look like and feel like our brand.

01:19.000 --> 01:20.000
So cool.

01:20.000 --> 01:23.000
Yeah. 5.5 was never capable of doing something along these lines.

01:23.000 --> 01:29.000
With 5.6, I spoke into it for five minutes and it output all of these different data slices that they needed.

01:29.000 --> 01:34.000
This feels like something you would normally think a big billion-dollar company could build.

01:34.000 --> 01:37.000
And you're like, we get this. I have my bespoke software system.

01:37.000 --> 01:41.000
Makes you feel real and enterprise-y.

01:41.000 --> 01:42.000
Yeah.

01:42.000 --> 01:44.000
It frees up the most important time for us.

01:44.000 --> 01:50.000
I get to choose where it goes, whether it's building the brand or spending time with my kids.

01:50.000 --> 01:53.000
And that to me is like the time I'll never get back.

01:53.000 --> 01:55.000
And so it's really exciting.

